---
/**
 * Participation terms for the field. The version date is stored with every
 * piece, so it is always clear which terms a contribution was made under.
 * Not legal advice — have these reviewed before public launch.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import EditorialNote from '../../components/EditorialNote.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.json';
const f = site.field;
---
<BaseLayout title="participation terms — the field" description="The terms for leaving a piece in the field, a participatory artwork by giles c mccrary iii.">
  <header class="page-head wrap">
    <a class="label" href="/field/">{f.title}</a>
    <h1>participation terms</h1>
    <p class="label">version {f.termsVersion}</p>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap prose terms">
    <EditorialNote>
      Draft for approval. These terms describe how the field is built and what it does, but
      they are not legal advice. Please have them reviewed before public launch. If they
      change, update the version date in settings → the field.
    </EditorialNote>

    <h2>1. what the field is</h2>
    <p>
      The field is a participatory artwork by {site.byline}, part of <em>{site.concept}</em>.
      Visitors abstract a word of their own and may choose to leave the result in the
      field, where it is shown together with pieces left by others. {site.byline} is the
      originating artist of the field. Each piece in it is a contribution by the visitor who
      made it, and is not created or individually endorsed by the artist.
    </p>

    <h2>2. what leaving a piece means</h2>
    <p>When you leave a piece in the field, you understand that:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>it becomes publicly visible on gilesmccrary.com, as part of the field;</li>
      <li>anyone may view it, link to it, and share it, including as an image carrying the field’s credit line;</li>
      <li>it remains visible until you remove it, or until it is removed in moderation;</li>
      <li>copies that others have already saved or shared cannot be recalled.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. ownership and licence</h2>
    <p>
      You keep any rights you have in the piece you make. The field does not take ownership
      of it.
    </p>
    <p>
      By leaving a piece, you grant {site.byline} a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free
      licence to display, reproduce, and share the piece as part of the field and its
      documentation: on this website, in exhibitions of the work, and in publications and
      records about the work. You also permit visitors to share the piece, with its credit
      line, through the sharing features the field provides.
    </p>
    <p>
      This licence lasts while the piece remains in the field. If the piece is removed, no
      new uses will be made of it, although documentation already created (for example,
      photographs of an exhibition) may remain.
    </p>

    <h2>4. what may not be left</h2>
    <p>Please do not leave anything that:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>is hateful, harassing, or threatening;</li>
      <li>impersonates the artist or anyone else;</li>
      <li>contains anyone’s personal information, such as names with contact details, addresses, phone numbers, or emails;</li>
      <li>contains links, advertising, or spam;</li>
      <li>you do not have the right to share.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Pieces are checked automatically, {f.moderation === 'pre' ? 'reviewed before they appear,' : 'can be reported by visitors,'}
      and may be hidden or removed at the artist’s discretion, without notice.
    </p>

    <h2>5. removing your piece</h2>
    <p>
      When you leave a piece, your browser keeps a private removal key for it. Open the piece
      from its link on the same device and choose “remove my piece”. If you no longer have
      the key (for example, after clearing your browser data), send the piece’s link through
      the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> and it will be removed.
    </p>

    <h2>6. privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Only the piece itself (its letters, their arrangement, and the date) is stored with
      your contribution. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> for everything that is
      processed when you take part, including by the site’s host.
    </p>

    <h2>7. no guarantee</h2>
    <p>
      The field is an artwork, offered as it is. It may change, pause, or end, and pieces may
      be rearranged in how they are shown.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .terms h2 { font-size: 1.375rem; margin-top: 2.25rem; }
  .terms ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; }
</style>
